Non-interactive status report over the closure, intended as a build gate.
Each port is classified as
.Cm ok ,
.Cm unconfigured
.Pq no saved options file ,
.Cm stale
.Pq the option list changed since the file was written, with the added and removed options named ,
or
.Cm conflict
.Pq the options make computes from the recorded ones, Va *_FORCE No and what Va IMPLIES No adds included, violate Va PREVENTS No or a group constraint .
Each
.Va PREVENTS
word is a pattern, matched against every option on, as the framework's
pre-check-config matches it; an option an
.Va IMPLIES
names goes in whether the port lists it or not, as
.Pa bsd.options.mk
adds it, and its own
.Va PREVENTS
is checked, an option
.Va OPTIONS_EXCLUDE
took out included.
Every flagged port also lists the options that
.Pa make.conf
does
.Em not
decide, as
.Ql undecided: ... ,
or is annotated
.Ql [mc-covered \[u2248]]
when
.Pa make.conf
decides all of them.
An unconfigured or stale port that is fully
.Cm mc-covered
does not demand attention (a conflict still does, and so does, under
.Fl s ,
a file synth would refuse), and blacklisted ports never do: poudriere will not
build them in this jail, tree and set, so their options cannot hold a build up.
Ports without any options are counted separately and not listed.
.Pp
A port caught in a dependency loop
.Pq see Sx Dependency loops
keeps its own status and gains a
.Ql [dependency loop]
annotation; the loop itself is named on standard error and counted in the
summary.
