Headless refresh of the options files over the closure: the fast equivalent of
.Nm poudriere Cm options Fl C .
For every port it keeps the saved file's choices for options that still exist,
adopts the effective value
.Pq defaults plus Pa make.conf
for options the file does not know about, and drops options that no longer
exist.
The file is read the way
.Pa bsd.options.mk
reads it: an option on both an
.Va OPTIONS_FILE_SET
and an
.Va OPTIONS_FILE_UNSET
line is off, and an option on neither, named only in
.Va _FILE_COMPLETE_OPTIONS_LIST ,
keeps its effective value.
Being a makefile, a hand-written file may name several options on one line,
put spaces around
.Ql +=
or
.Ql = ,
and assign a list afresh with
.Ql =
or
.Ql := ,
which drops what earlier lines added to it;
.Ql ?=
assigns only a list no earlier line of the file or its
.Pa options.local
assigned;
.Nm
reads it so, and writes it back the way
.Nm make Cm config
does, but for the
.Va _OPTIONS_READ
line, left out, and a longer
.Ql # Options for
comment
.Pq see Sx SYNTH .
A line ending in a backslash goes on over the next, as
.Xr make 1
joins them, a comment included.
An
.Pa options.local
beside the file is read after it, as
.Pa bsd.options.mk
does: its
.Va OPTIONS_FILE_SET
and
.Va OPTIONS_FILE_UNSET
lines join the file's, every SET entry of either applied before any UNSET
one, so an option on any UNSET line of either is off, and the result is the
saved choice every command shows and judges.
With no options file, an
.Pa options.local
is read after an empty one, so the options it decides are neither new nor
undecided.
.Cm sync
never writes or removes it, so what it unsets stays off whatever the options
file says; every command that reads one says so in a note naming the options
it sets or unsets.
An option one of its UNSET entries matches, as a pattern, cannot be edited
through the options file: the TUI and
.Cm decide
refuse it with
.Dq options.local decides Ar OPT ; edit it there .
Its SET entries lock nothing: each is a default the options file's UNSET
line overrides.
.Pp
Some options files
.Nm
cannot model, and leaves to
.Xr make 1 :
one whose
.Pa options.local
assigns
