is locked, with no
.Pa make.conf
verdict
.Pq see Cm scan Fl -options ;
and edits to it are refused.
An
.Va OPTIONS_FILE
outside the options directory for one flavor only leaves that flavor so, with its own outcome, while the
flavors still reading the shared file keep it managed, owned as below
whichever flavor the closure names first; the warning then names the port:
.Dl warning: OPTIONS_FILE is /elsewhere for misc/flav@nox, outside the options dir: make reads that file, not misc_flav/options, for it, and optique leaves its options alone
.Pp
.Cm sync
then reports every file it changed.
A port whose options file already records the same complete option list and the
same enabled set is left untouched; a changed package name alone does not force
a rewrite, matching
.Nm make Cm config-conditional .
A file that names an option with neither line, which
.Nm make Cm config
never writes, is warned about by every command that reads it and completed
by
.Cm sync :
.Xr make 1
reads such an option at its defaults, follows them if they change later, and
.Nm make Cm config-conditional
