.Pp
Options files belonging to ports that lost
.Em all
of their options are removed as dead configuration, but only when no port in
the closure sharing that options file still has options, so a flavor with an
empty option list never deletes the default flavor's file.
Removal deletes the
.Pa options
file and the containing directory, but keeps a user-managed
.Pa options.local
if one is present.
.Pp
All flavors of one origin share a single options file.
It is written from the default flavor's point of view, exactly as
.Nm make config
on the plain origin would; a non-default flavor that disagrees on an option
both flavors carry is reported as a warning rather than silently overwritten.
Disagreements confined to options one flavor does not even have, such as those
removed by
.Va OPTIONS_EXCLUDE ,
are structural and not reported.
An option a flavor takes out of the list through
.Va OPTIONS_SLAVE ,
as
.Pa databases/sqlite3@icu
does ICU, is on for that flavor with or without the file, as
.Nm make
has it.
When only non-default flavors of the origin are in the closure, the one with
the most options stands for the default flavor, and each option goes in with
the value of a flavor that has it; none ever drops what it does not see: the
file is up to date when everything each of them has is unchanged, none of its
options counts as obsolete, and a write keeps the list entry and
.Ql SET Ns / Ns Ql UNSET
line of every option those flavors lack as they were, since none can tell an
option it lacks from one the port removed; the default flavor's next write
drops the latter.
A flavor can set defaults of its own, which the shared file then overrides,
so a shared file is removed as repeating defaults plus
.Pa make.conf
only when it does so for every flavor reading it:
.Fl -minimal
judges the flavors in the closure,
.Cm clean Fl -redundant
queries every flavor in the port's
.Va FLAVORS ,
one
.Xr make 1
query each, and keeps the file when one of them cannot be queried.
A flavor whose
.Va OPTIONS_FILE
names another file reads none of the file and is not judged; a file no
flavor reads is kept.
.Pp
