.Sh CAVEATS
The query cache keys each answer on the files a
.Pa make.conf
pulls in with
.Ic .include
or
.Ic .sinclude
that
.Xr make 1
read for it, but a file a
.Ic .sinclude
skipped because it did not exist was not read: after creating one,
run once with
.Fl -clear-cache
.Pq or use Fl -no-cache
to have it seen.
.Pp
A git ports tree is known by its commit: a port edited in the tree and not
committed is not seen, and its cached answer stays.
Edit ports in an overlay, whose files are keyed by modification time
.Pq see Sx OVERLAYS ,
or run with
.Fl -no-cache
while editing.
.Pp
A cached answer is carried over a tree update when no file
.Nm make
read for it changed.
A port that
.Pa Mk/Uses/zig.mk
or
.Pa Mk/Uses/electron.mk
IGNOREd because the
.Pa lang/zig<N>
or
.Pa devel/electron<N>
port it asks for was not in the tree keeps that IGNORE once a later commit
adds the port, until the port itself or the
.Pa .mk
changes; run once with
.Fl -clear-cache
if such a port should have come back.
